What this covers
----------------
The game and everything in this repository — the code, the rules and
crosswords as the game plays them, the art (textures, icons, splash), the
music and sound effects and the scripts that make them — EXCEPT the files
listed below, which keep their own terms.

Michel Cheenne designed the game: its rules and its crosswords (taken
from his "GRILLE" sheets, see scripts/crossword_puzzles.gd;
his original documents are kept privately, not in this repository).
He gave Maximilien Naveau his permission, orally, during his lifetime;
his heirs' written agreement to these terms is being collected
(doc/autorisation_ayants_droit.typ).

Third-party files
-----------------
- assets/fonts/Caveat-Variable.ttf, Jost-Variable.ttf:
  SIL Open Font License 1.1 (Caveat-OFL.txt, Jost-OFL.txt beside them).
- data/dictionaries/: the French dictionary by Olivier R.
  (Dicollecte, "Classique" variant) and the word list made from it,
  Mozilla Public License 2.0 (README_dict_fr.txt).
- The music and sound effects are played by sampled instruments, none of
  them in this repository (the build downloads them), all free to use for
  making music: the classical guitar from the University of Iowa Musical
  Instrument Samples ("without restrictions"); the Salamander Grand Piano
  by Alexander Holm (CC-BY 3.0); the double bass, Meatbass by Karoryfer
  Samples (CC0); the clarinet and the flute from VSCO 2 Community Edition
  by Versilian Studios (CC0); the button accordion from FreePats (CC0). Their
  reverberation is the Brahmssaal of the Detmold University of Music,
  from the "Open Database of Spatial Room Impulse Responses at Detmold
  University of Music" by S. V. Amengual Gari, J. M. Arend,
  P. T. Calamia and P. W. Robinson (Zenodo, doi:10.5281/zenodo.4116247),
  CC-BY 4.0. See tools/audio/README.md.
